    "title": "<p><strong>Box&nbsp;14.07</strong> The International Cowden Consortium (ICC) operational diagnostic criteria {21194675}</p>",
    "legend": "",
    "source": "",
    "copyright": "Adapted from, Tan MH, Mester J, Peterson C, et al. A clinical scoring system for selection of patients for PTEN mutation testing is proposed on the basis of a prospective study of 3042 probands. Am J Hum Genet.88(1):42-56. Copyright 2011. With permission from Elsevier. PMID: 21194675",
    "tablehtml": "<table border=\"1\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td valign=\"top\" width=\"601\">\r\n<p><strong>Pathognomonic criteria</strong></p>\r\n<p>&bull; Adult Lhermitte&ndash;Duclos disease (cerebellar tumours)</p>\r\n<p>&bull; Mucocutaneous lesions</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; - Facial trichilemmomas, any number<sup>a</sup> (&ge;&nbsp;2&nbsp;biopsy-proven trichilemmomas<sup>b</sup>)</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; - Acral keratoses</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; - Papillomatous papules</p>\r\n<p>&bull; Mucosal lesions</p>\r\n<p>&bull; Autism spectrum disorder</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td valign=\"top\" width=\"601\">\r\n<p><strong>Major criteria</strong></p>\r\n<p>&bull; Breast cancer</p>\r\n<p>&bull; Non-medullary thyroid cancer</p>\r\n<p>&bull; Megalocephaly</p>\r\n<p>&bull; Endometrial carcinoma</p>\r\n<p>&bull; Mucocutaneous lesions<sup>b</sup></p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; - 1&nbsp;biopsy-proven trichilemmoma</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; - Multiple palmoplantar keratoses</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; - Multifocal cutaneous facial papules</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; - Macular pigmentation of the glans penis</p>\r\n<p>&bull; Multiple gastrointestinal hamartomas or ganglioneuromas<sup>b</sup></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td valign=\"top\" width=\"601\">\r\n<p><strong>Minor criteria</strong></p>\r\n<p>&bull; Other thyroid lesions (follicular adenomas, multinodular goitre)</p>\r\n<p>&bull; Mental retardation (i.e. IQ of &le;&nbsp;75)</p>\r\n<p>&bull; Gastrointestinal hamartomas<sup>a</sup> (single gastrointestinal hamartoma or ganglioneuroma<sup>b</sup>)</p>\r\n<p>&bull; Fibrocystic breast disease</p>\r\n<p>&bull; Lipomas</p>\r\n<p>&bull; Fibromas</p>\r\n<p>&bull; Genitourinary tumours (especially renal cell carcinoma)</p>\r\n<p>&bull; Genitourinary malformations<sup>a</sup></p>\r\n<p>&bull; Uterine fibroids</p>\r\n<p>&bull; Autism spectrum disorder<sup>b</sup></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td valign=\"top\" width=\"601\">\r\n<p><strong>Relaxed ICC operational diagnostic criteria for Cowden syndrome</strong></p>\r\n<p>&ge;&nbsp;1 pathognomonic criterion</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; <em>or</em></p>\r\n<p>&ge;&nbsp;2 major or minor criteria</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p><sup>a</sup>Present in this section as defined by ICC criteria only. <sup>b</sup>Present in this section as defined by National Comprehensive Cancer Network (NCCN) 2010 criteria only.</p>",
    "imageUrl": null,
